perf(arange): inline type-specific loops matching NumPy's template approach

Replace delegate-based FillArange<T> with inlined switch/case loops:
- Eliminates Func<double, T> delegate call overhead per element
- Matches NumPy's arraytypes.c.src template-generated fill functions
- Direct pointer casts: addr[i] = (int)(start + i * step)

NumPy's fill pattern (from arraytypes.c.src):
  @type@ delta = buffer[1] - buffer[0];
  for (i = 2; i < length; ++i)
      buffer[i] = start + i * delta;

Both implementations use simple scalar loops - no SIMD.
